SCENE — the entrance to a low pale apartment building on a clean residential street, seen dead-on: a simple recessed doorway, a couple of shallow steps, a palm tree, a clean kerb and a short stretch of pale paving in front. Warm, soft, late-afternoon sunlight — still bright and clear, never dusk, never orange. An empty marked parking bay is painted on the paving directly in front of the doorway, centred in the frame. No people.

The camera is level and square-on to the doorway, which sits centred in the frame.
@@A@@ The little green car is entering from the LEFT in profile, leading one ordinary grey family saloon behind it; the marked bay in front of the doorway is still empty.
@@B@@ The ordinary grey saloon is now parked squarely in the marked bay in front of the doorway, centred in the frame, seen three-quarter from the front. The little green car has pulled aside to the LEFT of the bay, angled away, clearly yielding the bay and the frame to the grey car rather than occupying it.
